{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt","id":1560852,"title":"crowd source ideas for the aranta-shadur (Nosferatu scavenger hunt)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-22T02:03:12-07:00","id":1560852,"title":"crowd source ideas for the aranta-shadur (Nosferatu scavenger hunt)","content":"Clanbook: Nosferatu described a particular clan ritual, the<i> aranta-shadur</i>. It is a game that provides practical training for clan members. The clan elders gather all the ancillae and neonates in the warren. Each participant is given their own list of items to acquire. Certain items are common to all lists while others are chosen specifically for that individual based on their own ability or to help develop a particular skill. Sometimes the exact same item (not duplicates of the item, but a unique item) is shown on two or more Nosferatu lists to spur competition. The people who own such items could be mortal or Kindred.<br /> <br /> The <i>aranta-shadur</i> stipulates that all items must be acquired without the knowledge or detection of its owner. Whichever Nosferatu acquires the most items on her list before the deadline (usually sunrise) wins the hunt. Afterwards, all items are returned, again to be accomplished without the knowledge of its owner.<br /> <br /> It's meant for fun and to help develop the espionage abilities of Nosferatu. Although not mentioned, I assumed there are some kind of &quot;prizes&quot; that act as mementos or prestige, but nothing too serious.<br /> <br /> It's a neat little flavor text for the clan. It's very evocative and potentially very fun for a Nosferatu player. It is also an interesting way to provide potential story hooks to a player. However, it is also an immense amount of work for an ST to do. The ST has to come up with an entire list for a Nosferatu PC (and possibly more than one), decide on possible challenges/scenarios to describe for one or more items, and provide some type of description of what the other Nosferatu NPCs have achieved as well. That's not beyond the capabilities for most STs, but it is a lot of work. We also must remember this is not a one time only event. It's something the local Nosferatu would do at least once a year, perhaps more. So it's not just doing it once, but potentially describing many such scavenger hunts over the course of a chronicle.<br /> <br /> Rather than just giving us two paragraphs, this is an area I really wish we got an old style random table chart with a hundred different items and a half dozen brief &quot;encounters&quot;. Not only would it cut down on the work needed, it would also inspire a lot more ideas from an ST. Particularly because regardless of how much time it might take IC, this is probably a scene most STs will complete in less than ten minutes of game time. It just needs a brief set up, providing a PC some kind of list, allowing them to narrate how they complete it, maybe give a specific story hook or clue for upcoming game session, and then narrating a conclusion. Despite that limited amount of time &quot;on screen&quot;, this can add a lot to the game for Nosferatu PCs, and even the other players can enjoy the scene as described.<br /> <br /> So I'm hoping the board members can contribute various ideas (of varying difficulty) on how to run this. What scavenger hunt items do you think would be good? Remember the idea is that int he process of obtaining the item, it is achievable, fun, and helps them develop spycraft skills.<br /> <br /> Here are some initial ideas of my own.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Expensive fountain pen of a local CEO (or Ventrue or ghoul/retainer/ally)</li> <li>Specific jewelry piece of a Toreador or local celebrity</li> <li>Index card/notepaper containing the computer passwords for a specific individual</li> <li>Musical instrument of a local musician</li> <li>A particular DVD/blu-ray movie/TV found in a person's house (from anybody, it's a test more of observation than planning)</li> <li>A cookie jar or other knick-knack showing a particular cartoon or comic strip character</li> <li>A particular perfume bottle that still contains the perfume in question</li> <li>A foreign language dictionary</li> <li>A used pizza box</li> <li>A particular kind of living pet (also tests Animalism)</li> <li>A shot glass with the name of its distiller or bar</li> <li>A used movie or concert ticket stub</li> <li>An item that contains an animal part of an endangered animal (like ivory)</li> <li>A milk carton that has been expired more than 1 month</li> <li>An old valentine's day card that has been kept for more than one month</li> <li>A high school prom garter</li> <li>An old bridesmaid dress</li> <li>A key to a specific model/make of car</li> <li>A t-shirt showing a specific affinity group identity</li> <li>A person's piece of clothing showing a sports team that is not local to the area</li> </ol>I'm interested in reading your own lists as well as other ideas for the <i>aranta-shadur</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T05:17:13-07:00","id":1560855,"title":"","content":"Oh, that sounds fun!<br /> <br /> As a suggestion, for actual play I would probably have a list with filler items and maybe one or two items that are slightly trickier to get.<br /> That way it can be assumed the character can get most of them (or roll Backgrounds/Abilities) and the hunt for the 'special' item can be played as representative of how they do overall. Playing complete lists would probably tire out quickly, especially if it is just one Nosferatu player at the table.<br /> <br /> Some suggestions for the list and reasons:<br /> <br /> - The weather report for [city], June 16th 1921 (paper trail, archives)<br /> - The favorite color of the Harpy (social engineering)<br /> - A specific type of fungus, in or around the warren (covering bases)<br /> - The name tag of a Jane or John Doe from a mortuary (infiltration)<br /> - A poem created from shredded office documents (dumpster diving)<br /> - Empty take-out coffee cup of a cop (trailing)<br /> - The signature of a mortal on a silly petition form (deception, subterfuge)<br /> - An imprint of the manhole cover on X Str / Y Ave (get creative)<br /> - Drug-free urine sample (streetwise)<br /> - A specific book that is out of print (library use, scrounging)<br /> - Date of birth of a random person (investigation)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T05:35:10-07:00","id":1560856,"title":"","content":"Mocking someones low humanity:<br /> <br /> 33. The most fragrant flower from a flower shop (logic: someone with low humanity has difficulty knowing what smells 'good')<br /> 34. A set of cozy beddings (yeah we know you've stopped caring about sleeping on a bed, we all know)<br /> 35. A puppy that has never tasted blood from the local pet store (low humanity: animals become more angsty and bark louder)<br /> <br /> Mocking someone's high humanity:<br /> 36 An infant, less than a month old (you'll get to hand it back... Probably)<br /> 37 Skeletal remains from a human. (A bone is fine, a whole Skeleton is extra points.<br /> 38 A recently drained rat (rat sucker, rat sucker rat sucker)<br /> 39 Golconda. (Check behind the couch)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T08:24:25-07:00","id":1560857,"title":"","content":"One way for an especially \u2026 testing \u2026 Elder to weed out those destined for a long run from the mere placers would be to list something everyday that sounds as though it should be found in the shops, but is in fact out of production and only found in a local museum (A certain make of tyre or a certain brand of cigarettes perhaps?).<br /> <br /> Not a big world-class museum, more a point of local pride.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Those looking to weed out the really meticulous and/or devious minds could list something that can be interpreted in more than one way (\u2018A coffin nail\u2019 could be literal or it could refer to a cigarette and exactly which a newbie chases after could reveal something about them).<br /> <br /> Another possible example of this would be an older British vampire asking for \u2018a half-crown\u2019 (Which might refer to a pre-decimal coin, a luckless tiara or something similar) or a \u2018bob\u2019 (Also a pre-decimal coin, but a photograph of somebody called \u2018Bob\u2019 or a wig in a certain hairstyle might be equally acceptable).<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019d suspect that most of these scavenger hunts would only list articles associated with vampires from other Clans when these are known to be non-Hostile (I.E. Will test the youngster, but not to destruction).<br /> <br /> - it is also a racing certainty that none of these prizes will be of the sort to cause Serious Problems for the local warren (Somebody asking for \u201cThe Prince\u2019s Pride\u201d, for example, would probably be asking for trouble in a way their peers would not approve of).<br /> <br /> - Finally, it does seem likely that there will be a mix of straightforward requests and riddles subtle &amp; blatant in the list, but that every item listed must be PORTABLE (Unless the local elder or elders are Real Jerks).<br /> <br /> An obvious point, I know, but probably useful to keep in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T11:56:42-07:00","id":1560893,"title":"","content":"First let's remember those are vampires: they can work on extended timescales and they can game any tradition for personal interest.<br /> <br /> I think the system must consider first the layers behind local tradition:<br /> <br /> 1. How frequent it is? 1/week to 1/decade.<br /> <br /> 2. How serious is it locally? Enough to reward or cost Social Backgrounds? To risk life?<br /> <br /> 3. What's the hidden goal? There might be none, but always good to think about it.<br /> <br /> 4. Who are favored or despised by organizers?<br /> <br /> 5. How competitive vs evaluative it is?<br /> <br /> Frequency greatly affects overall difficulty and prizes. Frequent tough challenges will just tire everyone, and tolerance for skipping will be higher. A once a decade game has everyone riled up for years ahead of time, and the prestige is naturally way higher.<br /> <br /> Seriousness affect how far they're willing to go for the game. It probably doesn't pay to ask for potential murder just for bragging rights, bad for the Masquerade. But if it is like a religious thing, a rite of passage or there's feeding rights at stake, the Nos as a whole may be willing to piss off the Prince seriously, and participants to face Final Death for even slight advantages.<br /> <br /> Hidden goals mean one or more organizers have hidden agendas, which means there's plot (even if minor) within the game. Some items may be intended for real, with a cover of deniability. Someone is to be punished or rewarded. Some items are tests of the safety of some areas or some persons. The point is, 1-3 items are actual plot points and the scenes will affect further developments.<br /> <br /> Favored and despised really just means if the organization is willing to rig the game, and how far. Even if the PC is neutral, this affects both description of results and how hard it is to beat the competition.<br /> <br /> Competitive vs Evaluative is another kind of consideration: how valuable is it to hit certain milestones regardless of final position? That will greatly affect the strategies of participants as priority changes from absolute to relative position.<br /> <br /> Notice: if local elders want to ensure the clan is capable at cooperating and put grudges aside for common safety, they'll value absolute position, the game is a place to show progress. If they want fierce competition and to either groom ruthless allies or pit the youngsters against each other, they'll greatly emphasize the 1st place and treat any performance below it as no better than total failure.<br /> <br /> I have more to brainstorm, but that's it for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T14:23:28-07:00","id":1560901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560855#post1560855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a suggestion, for actual play I would probably have a list with filler items and maybe one or two items that are slightly trickier to get.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of actual play, I would do as you suggest and have a number of filler items that are basically there just as flavor text. I would only have one or maybe two items where the PC could go into more detail. One could be a fairly quick scene meant to be played our just fun. The other would be something meant as an actual plot hook. In terms of taking up actual game time, I'd probably aim for 5-10 minutes total because I don't want the other players sitting around and doing nothing for too long.<br /> <br /> In terms of how many scavenger hunt items are acquired, I'd probably just ask the player which ones they think their PC would be able to do that night realistically and how they would do that (as a quick reality check). Like any scavenger hunt, some items can be done, but would take too much time. Then I'd run the one or two special quick scenes, and then count up the successes. I would then roll randomly to determine how many the other Nosferatu got. Personally, I like a 20 item list because I run 1d10+10 real quick for each of the NPCs, compare to the PC, and determine a &quot;winner&quot;. The winner, as I said, wins mostly prestige because this is mainly meant as fun activity that bonds the clan in a common culture while teaching them some useful skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560855#post1560855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some suggestions for the list and reasons:</div> </div> </div> </div>I like a lot of your suggestions, and the reasoning for each in parenthesis. That's exactly along the lines I was thinking of. I also like how not everything is a physical item, and some are actual information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T14:54:36-07:00","id":1560911,"title":"","content":"Some good questions. Here are my answers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560893#post1560893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. How frequent it is? 1/week to 1/decade.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is supposed to be a fun activity that helps the brood bond together and teach them useful skills. I imagine most broods do it at least once a year, perhaps several times during a year. Not so often that it becomes tiresome or a bother, and not too infrequent that it is no longer seen as a tradition or part of clan culture. I imagine it is usually tied to a Hosting with the <i>aranta-shadur</i> being known in advance. There is probably a traditional Hosting known for it on some kind of anniversary schedule (the first Hosting of the year, the one always held in October, etc.) It's supposed to be organized by the elders so the ancillae and neonates participate. If the hunt is not done on some kind of regular anniversary basis, I imagine when word goes out about the next Hosting, it's revealed that an <i>aranta-shadur</i> is planned.<br /> <br /> For STs, I'd keep it to whatever schedule makes the most for their game. If the PCs aren't that interested in it, keep it once a game year and hand wave it as background. If the PCs have a real fun for it, have it at whatever frequency it makes sense for the ST and players. I imagine for determining the actions of NPCs only, I'd determine something like 1-4 times. Small broods may do it only once a year while large broods may do it multiple times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560893#post1560893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. How serious is it locally? Enough to reward or cost Social Backgrounds? To risk life?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's supposed to be fun. Most items are on everyone's list with a few individual ones tailored to that Nosferatu's abilities. The clanbooks say when the elders really want to test the younger Nosferatu they simply put the same unique item on more than one Nosferatu's list.<br /> <br /> So certainly no risk to life or any other cost. I imagine there is some slight &quot;prize&quot; given as an award, and some temporary prestige to the Nosferatu who just won. A Nosferatu who consistently wins the <i>aranta-shadur</i> likely gains some permanent Clan Status/Prestige, but is eventually taken out of competition and asked to help organize the hunt. After all, it is no fun if the same person constantly wins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560893#post1560893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. What's the hidden goal? There might be none, but always good to think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the goal is just to test each brood member's stealth, cunning, investigation and espionage in a fun way. The clan wants to encourage these traits because it makes the brood stronger in collecting information.<br /> <br /> Individual hunts may indeed have a goal for the elders such as most items secretly involve a particular Ventrue's Influence holdings, involve the vampires of the Tremere chantry, or similar. Simply the act of collecting the items may reveal important information concerning something the clan elders want to know more about. That may or may not be known to the participants as a whole. Or it may be part of the test to see if one or more Nosferatu have figured out what the &quot;target&quot; is. For an ST, he only needs to bother with this if he wants that as a particular story hook for the PCs to follow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560893#post1560893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Who are favored or despised by organizers?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the scavenger hunt may be sandbagged so that a particular Nosferatu is sandbagged or given an edge, I probably wouldn't both with that myself. I don't think this activity is really about determining the winner. It's to have fun, create a bond and common culture, and encourage brood members to develops the skills the elders want them to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560893#post1560893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. How competitive vs evaluative it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Competitive enough to be fun, but not so competitive that it isn't fun. I imagine the elders don't even mind if some Nosferatu team up to work their lists together (especially when it is a relatively new embrace who needs to be mentored, or a recent arrival to the local Brood). I also think that doing the scavenger hunt in teams could be a good way for some game groups to keep all players involved by handing out some brief NPC descriptions and dice pools to each of the other players who have non-Nosferatu PCs. Every game group will be different in whether something like that works for them or not.<br /> <br /> I think the descriptions given in the clanbooks provide sufficient explanations for anyone wanting to run one in their chronicle. There is some slight wording differences between the original and revised clanbooks, but nothing important changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T14:55:47-07:00","id":1560912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560857#post1560857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Those looking to weed out the really meticulous and/or devious minds could list something that can be interpreted in more than one way (\u2018A coffin nail\u2019 could be literal or it could refer to a cigarette and exactly which a newbie chases after could reveal something about them).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an excellent suggestion and certainly in the spirit of really good real life scavenger hunts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T01:41:59-07:00","id":1560929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560911#post1560911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Individual hunts may indeed have a goal for the elders such as most items secretly involve a particular Ventrue's Influence holdings, involve the vampires of the Tremere chantry, or similar. Simply the act of collecting the items may reveal important information concerning something the clan elders want to know more about. That may or may not be known to the participants as a whole. Or it may be part of the test to see if one or more Nosferatu have figured out what the &quot;target&quot; is. For an ST, he only needs to bother with this if he wants that as a particular story hook for the PCs to follow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think generally there is no reason for the Nosferatu to not combine the fun with something useful. Especially hunts for (seemingly) innocuous bits of information present an opportunity to collect data that may prove useful in the long run. Or the scavenger hunt itself might serve as a deliberate distraction if the Nosferatu are suspecting they are under observation, for example.<br /> <br /> One tweak the book doesn't mention I thought of is to allow participants to submit one item of their own to the elders, who evaluate the viability and the put it on the list of another Clan member. That could help evaluating the mindset of a member, and it gives the player an opportunity to have their character get something they want in exchange. They will also have to consider what a reasonable task might be for their Clan members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T03:41:04-07:00","id":1560931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560929#post1560929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think generally there is no reason for the Nosferatu to not combine the fun with something useful. Especially hunts for (seemingly) innocuous bits of information present an opportunity to collect data that may prove useful in the long run. Or the scavenger hunt itself might serve as a deliberate distraction if the Nosferatu are suspecting they are under observation, for example.<br /> <br /> One tweak the book doesn't mention I thought of is to allow participants to submit one item of their own to the elders, who evaluate the viability and the put it on the list of another Clan member. That could help evaluating the mindset of a member, and it gives the player an opportunity to have their character get something they want in exchange. They will also have to consider what a reasonable task might be for their Clan members.</div> </div> </div> </div>You beat me to the suggestion that Clan Nosferatu might actually produce elders who ask their juniors for scavenger hunt suggestions!\ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> In that spirit, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Black Fox</a> , you could ask your own players for suggested additions to the list - and, in the proper \u2018Trickster Mentor\u2019 spirit, add a little twist that makes acquiring this item just a bit trickier to get at (For example, requiring that it come from a specific place or in a specific form).<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Also, this being Clan Nosferatu, there\u2019s always that one Elder who hates Beautiful People so much they ask for the contents of the hair from somebody\u2019s head or the clothes from their back* - though in all seriousness adding the camera of some famous fashion photographer or a local beauty queen\u2019s mirror or the knives of a plastic surgeon to the list seems perfectly in character (and a working camera could conceivably be useful to the brood, whilst surgical knives might be helpful in another way).<br /> <br /> Actually, a sliver of glass from a supermodel\u2019s mirror might be more Nosferatu-style (Since it requires the mirror be broken in the process of acquiring it).<br /> <br /> <br /> *\u201dLaundry basket is OK, wardrobe is cheating\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMax, we talked about this, we just want to scare the Beautiful People ****less, no need to make it creepy.\u201d<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T04:56:04-07:00","id":1560932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560931#post1560931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You beat me to the suggestion that Clan Nosferatu might actually produce elders who ask their juniors for scavenger hunt suggestions!\ud83d\ude0a<br /> <br /> In that spirit, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Black Fox</a> , you could ask your own players for suggested additions to the list - and, in the proper \u2018Trickster Mentor\u2019 spirit, add a little twist that makes acquiring this item just a bit trickier to get at (For example, requiring that it come from a specific place or in a specific form).<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Also, this being Clan Nosferatu, there\u2019s always that one Elder who hates Beautiful People so much they ask for the contents of the hair from somebody\u2019s head or the clothes from their back* - though in all seriousness adding the camera of some famous fashion photographer or a local beauty queen\u2019s mirror or the knives of a plastic surgeon to the list seems perfectly in character (and a working camera could conceivably be useful to the brood, whilst surgical knives might be helpful in another way).<br /> <br /> Actually, a sliver of glass from a supermodel\u2019s mirror might be more Nosferatu-style (Since it requires the mirror be broken in the process of acquiring it).<br /> <br /> <br /> *\u201dLaundry basket is OK, wardrobe is cheating\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMax, we talked about this, we just want to scare the Beautiful People ****less, no need to make it creepy.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with these suggestions is that it breaks that main stipulation of the hunt itself:<br /> <br /> &quot;The <i>aranta-shadur</i> stipulates that all items must be <b>acquired without the knowledge or detection of its owner</b>. Whichever Nosferatu acquires the most items on her list before the deadline (usually sunrise) wins the hunt. Afterwards, all items are <b>returned</b>, again to be accomplished <b>without the knowledge of its owner</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't return information, and if you break a mirror to get a sliver, well the owner is going to know something happened. Same with say someone's (living) hair. Secondly every item needs to be owned by someone or some entity. To use <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>'s list &quot;A specific book that is out of print (library use, scrounging)&quot; is perfectly within this idea where as &quot;A poem created from shredded office documents (dumpster diving)&quot; isn't since those shredded documents are now trash and in most situations be missed. &quot;The favorite color of the Harpy (social engineering)&quot; isn't feesable since it isn't a returnable item due to being just information, where as something like &quot;The Harpy's favorite colored shirt&quot; would be, and works twofold, finding the information and being an object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T15:47:00-07:00","id":1560951,"title":"","content":"Yes, the trick of the game is that the stipulations are not an excuse to cause chaos (in theory), but to test the ability to avoid doing so.<br /> <br /> This is what makes the Nos great information brokers: not only do they see things, but they can be trusted to leave no traces and to not rob you.<br /> <br /> Will the game be abused sometimes? Definitely. And while it's kind of implied that most failures take the form of giving up, some are definitely just caught red-handed.<br /> <br /> But the overall idea is to leave no trace of the game and no grievances against the Nosferatu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T18:08:52-07:00","id":1560952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560932#post1560932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't return information</div> </div> </div> </div>I would personally allow &quot;information&quot; as a list item provided there's some proof that the information is correct. I think the requirement that the item must be returned is less about it being a physical item that can be returned, and more about the idea that the person must never know they had been targeted. Meaning it's not enough the person does not realize they've been &quot;robbed&quot; by the deadline of the scavenger hunt, but that they never realize that it's happened. As long as that happens, I think it satisfies the requirement.<br /> <br /> For example, the &quot;Date of birth of a random person&quot; might be temporarily taking someone's driver's license, or xeroxing a credit card application form, or any number of things that shows someone's birth date. A driver's license must definitely be returned, but a photocopy of a credit card application need not be. Likewise a Nosferatu hacking into someone's computer and printing out a file that contains their birthdate would also be acceptable.<br /> <br /> Of course, if an ST demands in their chronicle that everything must be a physical item taken and returned, I wouldn't argue with the ST. Every ST is master of their chronicle world and determines how things are done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T18:32:51-07:00","id":1560954,"title":"","content":"Besides ideas of items that could be found on the list, I am interested in where people think the term &quot;<i>aranta-shadur</i>&quot; comes from. Does anyone recognize it as real words from some obscure language (perhaps using obsolete transliteration into the Latin alphabet)? Or is it made up fantasy nonsense that is supposed to represent an antediluvian tongue or a forgotten ancient language where the game was first invented?<br /> <br /> If we assume the term originated from the Nosferatu vampires already hiding from the Nictuku, it probably should be some term from a postdiluvian human language, likely from Mesopotamia.<br /> <br /> The game does introduce the occasional nonsense term like Tal'mahe'Ra, but I can't remember other cases of such, or decide whether all of them should be related in some manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T12:58:30-07:00","id":1560985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560932#post1560932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only problem with these suggestions is that it breaks that main stipulation of the hunt itself:<br /> <br /> &quot;The <i>aranta-shadur</i> stipulates that all items must be <b>acquired without the knowledge or detection of its owner</b>. Whichever Nosferatu acquires the most items on her list before the deadline (usually sunrise) wins the hunt. Afterwards, all items are <b>returned</b>, again to be accomplished <b>without the knowledge of its owner</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't return information, and if you break a mirror to get a sliver, well the owner is going to know something happened. Same with say someone's (living) hair. Secondly every item needs to be owned by someone or some entity. To use <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>'s list &quot;A specific book that is out of print (library use, scrounging)&quot; is perfectly within this idea where as &quot;A poem created from shredded office documents (dumpster diving)&quot; isn't since those shredded documents are now trash and in most situations be missed. &quot;The favorite color of the Harpy (social engineering)&quot; isn't feesable since it isn't a returnable item due to being just information, where as something like &quot;The Harpy's favorite colored shirt&quot; would be, and works twofold, finding the information and being an object.</div> </div> </div> </div> Dash it all, missed that bit - that\u2019s what you get after I speed read on a mobile phone screen.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> , my bet would be that it\u2019s a phrase the Nosferatu came up with themselves and that there\u2019s a certain amount of quiet competition amongst a number of Elders over the issue of who came up with it first - no, it wasn\u2019t them, but they\u2019d like to think it was one of their Sires.<br /> <br /> The closest thing to any scholarly consensus is that it was cooked up somewhere between what is now Russia and the Fertile Crescent, but none of the Old School will agree with anyone else\u2019s account of it\u2019s creation, it\u2019s exact etymology and it\u2019s precise meaning.<br /> <br /> The version most popular with the rest of the Clan is that the phrase was invented as part of a disinformation campaign intended to spook potent local rivals into thinking Clan Nosferatu were working with really, really Phenomenal Cosmic Powers when they were really just training up their fledgelings to avoid a level of close scrutiny that had previously diminished their numbers (With the phrase being passed from brood to brood to help create the impression the Phenomenal Cosmic Power was being spread throughout the Clan \u2026 and also for the amusement of various Nosferatu).<br /> <br /> As a result, it has become traditional for Nosferatu asked about the fiercely-contested meaning of the phrase to give listeners a story told with the strictest historic detail, solemn mien and gory details as they build up the historic significance and deep cultural meaning of the phrase, so that they can deliver their preferred interpretation into an atmosphere of suitable solemnity.<br /> <br /> One recent telling ended with \u201c\u2026 and now you are ready to know the meaning of this historic phrase: it means \u2018TOO GOOD TO BE TRUE, Sucker!\u201d, followed by the teller laughing his head off.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T13:03:08-07:00","id":1560986,"title":"","content":"Also, I am stone cold certain that whilst \u2018aranta-shadur\u2019 is just a phrase that\u2019s so old and ubiquitous only it\u2019s cultural significance remains, \u2018Tal\u2019mahe\u2019Ra\u2019 is what one would-be Vampire Tolkien cooked up when he (or she) was working to convince various Cainites that they didn\u2019t even have to speak a human language if they didn\u2019t feel like it (Something something \u201cLANGUAGE OF THE FIRST CITY!\u201d).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T17:56:54-07:00","id":1561179,"title":"","content":"Bumping this in the hope there are posters who will contribute more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560985#post1560985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest thing to any scholarly consensus is that it was cooked up somewhere between what is now Russia and the Fertile Crescent, but none of the Old School will agree with anyone else\u2019s account of it\u2019s creation, it\u2019s exact etymology and it\u2019s precise meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be the best approach. I agree that it's unlikely to be part of the same language that gave us Tal'mahe'Ra. That should be related somehow to the antediluvian First City. The Nosferatu progenitor is unlikely to have taught it to the childer he wants to eliminate. It likely dates to whatever Nosferatu spawned the rest of the clan outside the Nictuku. We don't need to go with an actual, documented ancient language with Sumerian. It could easily be from some language spoken by illiterate people that's been long lost. Just call it &quot;the Old Tongue&quot; and leave it at that.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if there are any other bits of strange language associated with Clan Nosferatu. Nothing springs to mind, but that doesn't mean something isn't already out there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T18:10:21-07:00","id":1561181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1561179#post1561179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder if there are any other bits of strange language associated with Clan Nosferatu. Nothing springs to mind, but that doesn't mean something isn't already out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>My suggestion: make it subterranean in origin.<br /> <br /> Whatever people spoke this language in the past, if they're even human, the Nosferatu met them because of living in caves and the like.<br /> <br /> It may even be that the clan took the tradition whole-cloth from this people, whomever lived in the bowels of the Earth hiding from humans before the arrival of vampires.<br /> <br /> They may even still be around, practicing the same tradition still and talking in this language that was never heard by the light-dwellers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T23:16:28-07:00","id":1561185,"title":"","content":"Some Nosferatu never go to the surface. An isolated community may see some language drift over time. Though they live indefinitely so I'd be very slow. Perhaps some of them speak really old versions of modern languages though, including long forgotten regional dialects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T05:05:22-07:00","id":1561189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tjalei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1561185#post1561185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Nosferatu never go to the surface. An isolated community may see some language drift over time. Though they live indefinitely so I'd be very slow. Perhaps some of them speak really old versions of modern languages though, including long forgotten regional dialects</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a lot of language drift can happen, they're not an isolated community: that's defined by a lack of contact with others, but the Nosferatu have such contact by nature and necessity, with other vampires and with mortals.<br /> <br /> The fact some never leave doesn't change this status: they may be isolated individuals, but the community isn't, and they still talk with their peers.<br /> <br /> But the notion holds, not despite that, because of that. As their own communities, Nosferatu is the most likely clan to produce an independent, internal language spoken in the warrens. This would borrow freely from other languages, but adapt to its own system. Exchange don't make languages necessarily more mutually intelligible, nor necessarily kills old words.<br /> <br /> In this scenario, the Aranta-Shadur could as a word have developed at any point in time, from any combination of languages, and still be part of a stable lexicon unique to the Nos.<br /> <br /> For such a scenario, I think the cultural spread would be similar to modern Arabic: you have a Standard language centered around important written records that are kept untranslated for this very reason, and local variants that may be barely mutually intelligible, but preserve a core lexicon and structure.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the untranslated texts mean that everyone is formally educated in Standard form and have ample written use for it, so it do work as a Lingua Franca.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T11:58:11-07:00","id":1561197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1561181#post1561181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever people spoke this language in the past, if they're even human, the Nosferatu met them because of living in caves and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea. We even have canonical candidates (like Vhujunka) in the larger WoD setting although their identity i's certainly not limited to those candidates. Of course, none of that would ever come into play unless the ST decided on a very unusual chronicle. But as flavor text, being told that the term supposedly came from &quot;little people&quot;, &quot;morlocks&quot;, &quot;dwellers from the earth,&quot; or whatever term is used for the underground people would have a very different feel than that is was some dead language spoken north of Sumeria.<br /> <br /> Of course, if the term does come from some underground creatures/people, I feel the ST should create some additional terms for aspects of Nosferatu specific culture as I think such an encounter would unlikely to have left just this one term.<br /> <br /> It also provides the option for the ST to create additional evidence of the language or the underground people that the Nosferatu clan would be interested in collecting. As unlike a dead language thousands of years long gone, the underground people could still exist, and the Nosferatu might have reason to try to resume communication.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I would personally go down this route for my chronicles, but it is an intriguing option.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T13:16:34-07:00","id":1561198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1560932#post1560932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem with these suggestions is that it breaks that main stipulation of the hunt itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I missed that. I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> that I would consider information in the spirit of the sport, but combining information acquisition with and item is the more elegant solution. The only problem I see with that is that restricting it strictly to items would restrict the possible scope of skills that could be trained. I also think the examples of the Clan Book are really tall orders, especially infiltrating the Havens of (possibly) multiple kindred twice.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> A few more items:<br /> <br /> - A breached website user/password list from the dark web (computer use)<br /> - The security pass of a low-level employee (impersonation)<br /> - The key to a city maintenance area (safe spaces)<br /> - Blueprints of public Building X (resource access)<br /> - Client files of a corporate lawyer (blackmail)<br /> - A random package from the customs office (interception)<br /> - Official stamp of a DMV clerk (forgeries)<br /> - Live video stream of an Elysium's parking lot (surveillance)<br /> - A trichobezoar (rare item acquisition)<br /> - A metal item from a magpie's nest (Animalism)<br /> - A flaked-off piece of flag blue pool coating (trolling)<br /> - Spare high voltage resistor from a substation (sabotage)<br /> - Recording of a number station transmission this night (coms)<br /> - Screenshot of comments/reposts on a planted ridiculous fake news article (misinfo)<br /> - A prepared specimen from a museum collection (artifact extraction)<br /> <br /> I think placing the items in places a Nosferatu would need access to semi-regularly makes sense as a means of maintenance; public registries, the morgue, hospital, etc.<br /> Reading back on my list, it's very dry. There is probably a way to add more fun twists while keeping the practicality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T13:24:05-07:00","id":1561199,"title":"","content":"Regarding the name Aranta-Shadur, I think it's.. a way to make <i>Shadow Errant </i>sound a bit cooler. I looked at Akkadian and Sanskrit but found no real matches. From an in-game perspective though, I like the 'deep ones language' idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T14:41:28-07:00","id":1561201,"title":"","content":"More good suggestions for the list. Thanks very much!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1561198#post1561198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think the examples of the Clan Book are really tall orders, especially infiltrating the Havens of (possibly) multiple kindred twice</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so as well. I do think that is something much easier with fairly young fledglings and neonates than older Kindred. Havens tend to be fairly simple at first, but get more elabaorate as characters (and players) gain more experience and resources. I imagine most Kindred targets of the scavenger hunts are these much younger, less powerful, and less experienced Kindred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1561198#post1561198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading back on my list, it's very dry. There is probably a way to add more fun twists while keeping the practicality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most of the items for the scavenger hunt should probably be dry. After all, almost every brood in the world will be having such hunts at least once a year. Sheer repetition will result in a lot of mundane items. However, the ST will want some some more interesting/tailored items that appear on a list to enliven the experience overall, or to serve as an interesting scene or plothook.<br /> <br /> I think even having a large list of mundane, dry items will help people craft more interesting variations.<br /> <br /> For example, I think a lot can be done with extracting a museum piece in storage (not on display since that would be too quickly noticed). Lots of variations can be done with the type of artifact, the organization which has it, and its actual physical location in storage. Likewise a specific kind of animal which may not be native to region or domesticated. You can involve zoos, exotic pet stores, invasive species, farms, mansions that have exotic pets, etc. If the clan elders knoww there is only one boa constrictor over ten feet long in the city, not only is such a target interesting, it'll create competition.<br /> <br /> Another easy variant is to assign different points to certain items than others. It would call out their perceived rarity or importance of developing that skill. There might even be some kind of handicap system so less skilled Nosferatu are encouraged to participate (and thus gain practical experience). Thus even the newly released neonate has a chance against a skilled aniclla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1561198#post1561198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From an in-game perspective though, I like the 'deep ones language' idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just realized that the Clanbooks also detail the level six Discipline power Song of the Dark which can summon forgotten or mysterious underground creatures that tend towards fantasy/horror/legend. Tying in the term aranta-shadur to creatures that get occasionally summoned to warrens by use of that elder power preserves a sense of continuity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T03:10:43-07:00","id":1561223,"title":"","content":"Apologies for not having more ideas \u2026 wait a minute, what if it\u2019s something of a tradition for Nosferatu elders to create \u2018time capsules\u2019 towards which they can point future participants in the aranta-shadur? (In a generation or three).<br /> <br /> Whilst the general location would be known, the youngsters would still face the challenge of reconnoitring the location and working their way around (or through) the obstructions which may have grown up over the years.<br /> <br /> This scenario could double the fun, because it may inspire the PCs to set up their own \u2018time capsule\u2019 and imagine what the world will look like when they come back for it (Heck, given your LA scenario is set circa AD 1992 you could show the PCs going after a hoard that was secreted in the US Bicentennial year and flash forward to an arnta-shadur set in AD 2026).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T08:28:15-07:00","id":1561239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1561223#post1561223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what if it\u2019s something of a tradition for Nosferatu elders to create \u2018time capsules\u2019 towards which they can point future participants in the aranta-shadur?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping with the rules, they could even state that the capsule must be returned, not only to return the place to pristine conditions, but to leave it for future games.<br /> <br /> They can also keep tabs of when each was found, giving more points for capsules that haven't been found in a long time.<br /> <br /> Add to the challenge that others can find those capsules, so the challenge includes tracking them and sometimes even reassembling them from scattered content.<br /> <br /> It does though demand the content to not give away any Nosferatu secret if found.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T12:24:51-07:00","id":1561250,"title":"","content":"Books in unique or long dead (on the surface) languages deliberately kept that way for security and to maintain the language is a pretty cool thing. Could spin a story off that, one of the books fall into the hands of a mortal scholar (the nosferatu who transported it fell upon misfortune). The scholar spends month painstakingly decoding and translating the time growing increasingly disturbed, and all the time the Nosferatu tries to track it down.<br /> <br /> <b>More items:</b><br /> By nature or demeanor; How well it fits is determined - certainly neutral and with no favoritism - by the elders.<br /> <br /> Architect<br /> What best represents the future<br /> <br /> Autocrat<br /> The quality of a leader.<br /> <br /> Bon Vivant<br /> A good time.<br /> <br /> Bravo<br /> Fear.<br /> <br /> Capitalist<br /> What's truly valuable (gold, it's gold)<br /> <br /> Caregiver<br /> Something to soothe the soul.<br /> <br /> Celebrant<br /> That which inspires.<br /> <br /> Chameleon<br /> Outdo anothers item.<br /> <br /> Child<br /> What you like the most.<br /> <br /> Competitor<br /> That which conquer.<br /> <br /> <b>By clan/character</b> - more actual items here:<br /> <br /> Ventrue Viktors Suit<br /> Brujah Bobs aviator glasses<br /> Malkavian Maximilians medication, wait he has none, get his self portrait instead.<br /> Toreador Tinas autograph, bonus points if it's on a picture of her<br /> Tremere Teds car (it's not like he ever uses it, also neonates; don't go into his chantry the gargoyles will get you)<br /> Gangrel Gunters boots<br /> Nosferateu neds nothing, he's also in the scavenger hunt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T22:21:12-07:00","id":1561338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560852-crowd-source-ideas-for-the-aranta-shadur-nosferatu-scavenger-hunt?p=1561223#post1561223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">wait a minute, what if it\u2019s something of a tradition for Nosferatu elders to create \u2018time capsules\u2019 towards which they can point future participants in the aranta-shadur? (In a generation or three).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is another interesting idea, and I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">monteparnas</a> comments on it.<br /> <br /> However, I am having a hard time developing it into good specifics for play. Details matter because they turn interesting ideas into either exciting or disappointing scenes during actual play.<br /> <br /> First, if this is just &quot;find the time capsule&quot; then is it a matter of figuring out clues and riddles to its location? Is that the challenge? (Presumably the clan elders know their precise location and monitor them to make sure they can be found in 20 or 30 or 50 years time or whatever the time length is.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8-YjKOWbf7g\" data-code=\"8-YjKOWbf7g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/8-YjKOWbf7g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Second, what should the the time capsule be carrying? I'm of the firm opinion that must time capsules (in real life) just have useless junk in them. What contents could they have that would be of any interest to the Nosferatu? Historical information isn't likely to be of use to the Nosferatu. If there is useful information in it, it should probably be preserved in a way that is always accessible. So these would probably just be curiosity items that might have some relevance in understanding the history of the warren, but not in any way that may jeopardize the Masquerade or warren security. So tokens of mementos of previous (and possibly still existing) Nosferatu of the warren. And remember that a long standing member of the warren will see these same items multiple times over their existence as a vampire. These mementos should be something they enjoy perusing again and again, but not so much that they'd prefer to keep it with them instead of in a capsule. In this scenario, while one Nosferatu (or group in a team effort style hunt) will get bragging rights to having found it, going over the capsule is probably meant as a bonding ritual for the local Brood as ancillae and elders explain what the various bits mean.<br /> <br /> At least that is how I am currently thinking about it. Interested in other opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T02:06:48-07:00","id":1561377,"title":"","content":"I think the mementos is the way to go. The objects are just curious at best, but going through the capsule the elders tell their history, which is more valuable.<br /> <br /> They could include mementos from members of the Warren who met Final Death, or who left for somewhere else. Collective mementos from events or periods that affected everyone. Mementos brought, along with their history, from other Warrens. And things from other Vampires as an excuse to talk about them and their secrets.<br /> <br /> Finding them could involve some clue or riddle, but the real challenge is to find out what happened to the capsule: was something built atop it? Is it now a military base? Who lives in that house today? Was it moved? Was it found? Is it now in a museum? What if it is out of immediate reach? The Nos may take care to avoid this, sure, but they may also want to see how the participants figure out ways to bring it back or present an alternative that counts. It would be entirely within the spirit of Vampire that the Elders expect the younger vampire to manipulate events and arrange things so the bearer of the time capsule will be in town with it by the time of the Aranta-Shadur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T10:05:44-07:00","id":1561383,"title":"","content":"It also seems logical to suggest that at least some of these \u2018time capsules\u2019 could serve a secondary purpose by holding something rivals and/or antagonists of the Nosferatu warren could conceivably value: nothing to start a war over, but a trophy that could conceivably be used to bait the said rival and/or opponent.<br /> <br /> By making these items part of the aranta-shadur the Warren keeps alive the knowledge, whilst also testing the security of it\u2019s hiding place AND rotating that hiding place on a regular basis makes it harder for opponents to track down.<br /> <br /> <br /> NOTE: It seems unlikely that these items would retain their potency forever, but even after they stop being potentially useful bait they might well make worthy trophies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}